  "id": "Compound::DB01053 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Benzylpenicillin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Slc22a6, which is a key player in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with varying scores indicating a robust and reliable relationship. Slc22a6 is involved in multiple transport activities, including sodium-independent organic anion transmembrane transport and anion:anion antiporter activity, all of which are directly linked to the function of Slc22a11. These pathways suggest that benzylpenicillin may influence the activity of Slc22a11 through the regulation of anion transport, potentially affecting the uptake or efflux of certain molecules across cell membranes. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between benzylpenicillin and Slc22a11, particularly through the modulation of anion transport processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc22a11 as a downstream effector in the transport cascade initiated by benzylpenicillin.",
